---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import Workflow from '../components/Workflow.astro';
import '../styles/home.css';

const loop = [
  {
    title: 'Understand',
    text: 'Your message, the conversation so far, and context you have allowed (the time, an attached file, the active app if granted) become one request to the model you chose.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Plan',
    text: 'For work with several steps, Lumo writes a plan you can see, and keeps it updated as it goes. When something important is missing it asks a structured question with options instead of guessing.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Act',
    text: 'The model asks to use a tool. Lumo’s core, not the model, checks the request: is the input valid, is this folder or account granted, what tier is it, has the rate limit been reached? Only then does it run, or ask you first.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Verify',
    text: 'Tools return evidence such as file paths and hashes, HTTP status codes or the IDs of things created. Write tools read back what they wrote. A step whose tool failed can never be reported as done.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Report',
    text: 'You get the answer plus a short summary of the steps taken, the tools used and the outcome. Every step is saved, so an interrupted task is marked as interrupted, never as successful.',
  },
];
---

<Base title="How Lumo works" description="How Lumo turns a request into a checked result: understanding, planning, tools gated by permission tiers, verification and a clear report.">
  <PageHead
    eyebrow="How Lumo works"
    title="Tell Lumo what you want. Lumo figures out how to make it happen."
    lede="Behind every answer is the same loop: understand, plan, act within your permissions, check the result, report back. Here is what happens at each step, and what Lumo will not do."
  />
  <div class="container">
    <section aria-labelledby="loop-title">
      <h2 class="h-display group-title" id="loop-title">The loop</h2>
      <ol class="steps-list">
        {
          loop.map((s) => (
            <li>
              <div>
                <h3 class="h3">{s.title}</h3>
                <p>{s.text}</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="wf-title">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 class="h-display" id="wf-title">Follow one request</h2>
        <p class="lede">An example request, step by step.</p>
      </div>
      <Workflow />
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="who-title">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 class="h-display" id="who-title">Who decides what</h2>
        <p class="lede">Lumo is split so that the part that talks to the model never holds the power to act on its own.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <div class="panel">
          <h3 class="h3">The model</h3>
          <p>Chooses among the tools it is offered and writes text. A tool call from the model is a request, nothing more.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <h3 class="h3">Lumo’s core</h3>
          <p>A native process that holds your keys and the database, validates every tool call and makes the final decision against your grants and the risk tier.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <h3 class="h3">You</h3>
          <p>Grant access, approve changes, and confirm sensitive actions in a system dialog that the app’s interface cannot create or answer.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="untrusted-title">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 class="h-display" id="untrusted-title">Web pages and files cannot give orders</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Content Lumo reads from the web, your files, email or screenshots is labelled as untrusted data before the model sees it. Permissions are
          never expressed in that context at all, so even text written to trick an AI cannot widen what Lumo is allowed to do: a sensitive action
          still needs your confirmation, and a tool call outside your grants still fails.
        </p>
        <p>
          Purchases, sends and deletions show their exact details in the confirmation, so a change slipped in by a web page would be visible to you
          before anything happens. Each task also has limits on tool calls, time and estimated spend.
        </p>
        <p><a href="/security/">Read the security and privacy overview</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
